  "_comment": "Chainlink USD price-feed aggregator proxies for the ChainlinkPriceOracle (src/oracle/ChainlinkPriceOracle.sol). Only the 5 chains with an existing deployment are covered. Per feed: `aggregator` = the AggregatorV3Interface proxy to pass to setFeed; `feedDecimals` = the feed's own decimals() (informational — the contract reads it on-chain); `publishedHeartbeat` = the feed's heartbeat exactly as published in the official Chainlink reference-data-directory (provenance only — never pass this to setFeed); `heartbeat` = the staleness bound actually written on-chain, which is `publishedHeartbeat + min(2 * publishedHeartbeat, 900)`. THE PAD IS NOT OPTIONAL: the published heartbeat is the interval at which a new round is *triggered*, but `updatedAt` lands ~15s later (round negotiation + transmission + L2 inclusion), so a bound equal to the published heartbeat is unreachable by construction — a feed cannot be fresher than it publishes, and any feed that actually reaches its heartbeat would read stale, closing the fail-closed operator-swap gate (task_045). Capping the pad at +900s keeps the 24h feeds at ~24h so the guard does not go slack where it was never tight. NOTE: setFeed(currency, aggregator, heartbeat, tokenDecimals) is keyed by the managed TOKEN address (per pool config), not by symbol — map each pool token to its asset symbol here, and pass the TOKEN's own decimals as tokenDecimals. Aggregators and publishedHeartbeat verified from Chainlink reference-data-directory JSON (aggregators 2026-07, heartbeats re-verified 2026-08 — all 68 rows matched). test/SetOracleFeeds.t.sol lints the pad on every row. See script/README.md.",

